From 3ccf8b8a6a10616f4c4b7f0376d2217f7235050c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:34:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] feat(posix): trap device registers on arm64 and x86-64
 linux

AddVectoredExceptionHandler now installs a SIGSEGV/SIGBUS handler that
builds the EXCEPTION_RECORD Windows would (write flag, fault address) and
passes the ucontext as the CONTEXT. mmio_decode.h decodes the faulting
instruction on both hosts: the existing x86-64 decoder reads the ucontext
registers, and a new A64 decoder covers LDR/STR of every width and
addressing mode, LDP/STP, LDAR/STLR/LDAPR and the FP/SIMD forms.

The OHCI, NV2A and APU hooks use it on Linux, the AC'97 and watch traps
emulate the store instead of single-stepping it, and host.c builds on
POSIX without the D3D8 window. Also adds GetComputerNameA, _putenv_s and
SetUnhandledExceptionFilter to the shim, and links libm into it.
